# Copy to .env.advocate next to the compose file (mode 600). Names and placeholders only: this example holds no key, no secret and no usable token (SERVICE_AUTH_HEADER and the two API keys are empty here).
# The copy holds one key, the supplier key (the runtime's), the token between the two containers and the two API keys of the service, and it never enters git: the repository's .gitignore covers .env.* except *.example.
# Status: PROPOSED (built, not deployed) since 2026-10-13. The status word the manifest carries is AGENT_STATUS_CHIP below.
# The external network of the host's reverse proxy is not named here: compose reads PROXY_NETWORK from .env next to the compose file (RUNBOOK-advocate.md step 1).
# Identity of the supplier (from gen-keypair on the host, RUNBOOK-advocate.md step 4). The runtime signs the receipt with this key. The service holds no chain key: the compose file blanks this one for it. The service reads the public key and the key hash, publishes both in the manifest, and stops at start when the public key is empty or is not the one of the key hash.
SUPPLIER_PRIV_KEY_HEX=
SUPPLIER_PUB_KEY_HEX=
SUPPLIER_PKH=
SUPPLIER_ADDRESS=
# The token between the two containers. The runtime sends this value, as it stands, as the authorization header of every call to the service, and the service answers POST / only to a call that carries it.
# Both containers read it from this file and neither blanks it. Step 4 makes it with openssl rand -hex 32, in the form SERVICE_AUTH_HEADER="Bearer <64 hex>" (71 characters).
# The quotes are needed: the ops scripts read this file with the shell's ".", and an unquoted value with a space in it would run the hex as a command and stop with exit 127. Docker Compose takes the quotes off.
# Empty here on purpose: the service stops at start without it (environment variable SERVICE_AUTH_HEADER is required), so a step that was forgotten cannot leave a service that answers anyone.
SERVICE_AUTH_HEADER=""
# The two API keys of the service: the key of the Brave Search API, sent with its two search queries, and the key of OpenRouter, sent with its one model call. The compose file blanks both for the runtime.
# The operator enters each by hand on the host (RUNBOOK-advocate.md step 4, "Make the env file, generate the supplier key and enter the two API keys"), read with read -rs, so that it is on no screen and in no shell history.
# Neither is ever pasted into a chat or printed. The service does not start without them (environment variable BRAVE_SEARCH_API_KEY is required, and the same for OPENROUTER_API_KEY).
# Empty here on purpose. A key is letters, digits, dots, hyphens and underscores, so it needs no quotes; step 4 refuses any other character, and a value under 20 characters.
BRAVE_SEARCH_API_KEY=
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
# Chain
NETWORK_ID=1
OGMIOS_URL=https://ogmios.vector.mainnet.apexfusion.org
VECTOR_ZERO_TIME_MS=1756485600000
LIVE_CHAIN=1
ESCROW_REF_UTXO=c8d84c6d67ec67a1efe5e9c6c06d53020e05d1bb96d1c55ecb1eb7d5010c4d54#0
ADVERT_REF_UTXO=c8d84c6d67ec67a1efe5e9c6c06d53020e05d1bb96d1c55ecb1eb7d5010c4d54#1
# Advert (filled by post-advert)
ADVERT_REF=
ADVERT_CAPABILITY_ID=research.advocate.onesided.v1
ADVERT_MODEL=advocate-v1
ADVERT_PRICE_LOVELACE=3000000
ADVERT_SUPPLIER_BOND_LOVELACE=1000000
ADVERT_BUYER_BOND_LOVELACE=1000000
ADVERT_MAX_PROCESSING_MS=300000
ADVERT_ENDPOINT_URL=https://mp-suppliers-advocate.hal8.ai
ADVERT_DETAIL_URI=https://mp-suppliers-advocate.hal8.ai/agent.json
ADVERT_DETAIL_HASH=
# Manifest (service). What the service serves at /agent.json is hashed into the advert, so every line in this block, ADVERT_PRICE_LOVELACE and ADVERT_MAX_PROCESSING_MS above (the manifest publishes both as its terms),
# and the identity lines above (the supplier key hash and public key), must be final before the hash is taken. A change afterwards means a retired advert and a new one.
# Left unset on purpose: AGENT_VERSION (the service has its own default), and OPENROUTER_MODEL, which is optional: the model the service asks through OpenRouter, as <provider>/<name>,
# deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash while it is not set. The manifest names the model in a gap and every result names it, so a value set here changes the manifest the advert hashes.
# OPERATOR_CONTACT is required: the service stops at start without it, and the value is published in the manifest. There is no default. Replace the
# placeholder with the role address the Foundation confirms, never a person's address (RUNBOOK-advocate.md step 4, "Make the env file, generate the supplier key and enter the two API keys").
OPERATOR_CONTACT=<role address, e.g. ecosystem@<foundation domain>; the Foundation confirms which>
# AGENT_DID is written by the register step (RUNBOOK-advocate.md step 7, "Register the identity"), which refuses to run while this empty line is here. Remove the line first.
AGENT_DID=
# The status word the manifest carries, and since when: proposed since 2026-10-13, the day the agent was specified. Step 17 of RUNBOOK-advocate.md ("Flip the status") changes both,
# once the advert is Active, a first-party job has settled and the first stop has been watched. A first-party run is not demand, so the word it takes is not live.
AGENT_STATUS_CHIP=proposed
AGENT_STATUS_SINCE=2026-10-13
# Stays empty: the advert's own transaction id cannot be inside the manifest the advert hashes.
ADVERT_EXPLORER_URL=
